{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Florida black bear ("Ursus americanus floridanus") is a subspecies of the American black bear that has historically ranged throughout most of Florida and southern portions of Alabama, Georgia, and Mississippi.","title":"Florida black bear"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The large black-furred bears live mainly in forested areas and have seen recent habitat reduction throughout the state.","title":"Florida black bear"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Japanese black bear ("Ursus thibetanus japonicus") is a subspecies of the Asian black bear that lives on three main islands of Japan: Honshu, Shikoku and Kyushu.","title":"Japanese black bear"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" There are said to be 10,000 black bears on Japan.","title":"Japanese black bear"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The population of black bears on Shikoku and Kyushu may be endangered or extinct.","title":"Japanese black bear"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" There is a high price on bear parts in the black market, which threatens all bear populations in Japan.","title":"Japanese black bear"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" This particular species of bear are typically smaller with males only reaching 60-120 Kg and females only weighing about 40-100 Kg.","title":"Japanese black bear"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Their body length is about 120–140 cm long.","title":"Japanese black bear"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Ursus americanus
